1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,537
and it teaches no new word.

3
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:12,250
You're going to write your own long away mission.

4
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,628
Three areas, a quest tree, and two endings.

5
00:00:17,078 --> 00:00:21,426
Three jobs, each with something only that person can do.

6
00:00:23,226 --> 00:00:26,270
I'll show you mine, start to finish.

7
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:31,502
It's small on purpose, so you can read all of it.

8
00:00:33,302 --> 00:00:35,041
Then you write yours.

9
00:00:36,241 --> 00:00:41,459
Start on paper, with the same three sentences as the sixth lecture.

10
00:00:42,359 --> 00:00:45,837
The question, and the answer found in pieces.

11
00:00:46,287 --> 00:00:48,896
And the choice at the end.

12
00:00:50,696 --> 00:00:52,435
Mine is a mine.

13
00:00:52,885 --> 00:00:55,493
Four diggers behind a rock fall.

14
00:00:56,393 --> 00:00:59,437
Dig them out and keep the mine,

15
00:00:59,887 --> 00:01:02,930
or blast them out and lose it.

16
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:07,774
Then the beat sheet from last time.

17
00:01:08,674 --> 00:01:11,283
A landing, three tracks, a join,

18
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:14,341
a last area, and an ending.

19
00:01:14,791 --> 00:01:16,965
With minutes beside each one.

20
00:01:18,165 --> 00:01:20,774
Three areas, and one decision each.

21
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:24,283
The camp is where they land.

22
00:01:25,183 --> 00:01:28,661
The lift house has to be found once.

23
00:01:29,111 --> 00:01:32,589
After that the ship can put you there.

24
00:01:33,489 --> 00:01:37,402
And the gallery can't be beamed into at all.

25
00:01:37,852 --> 00:01:40,461
That's what makes the lift matter.

26
00:01:42,261 --> 00:01:45,739
Look at the map with last week's eyes.

27
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:50,117
Every mark is the name of a place.

28
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:53,176
Nothing hidden stands on a mark.

29
00:01:54,076 --> 00:01:58,424
And the titles read well after the words go to.

30
00:01:59,624 --> 00:02:03,537
Draw three columns before you write a single prop.

31
00:02:03,987 --> 00:02:06,596
Who's doing what, in each beat?

32
00:02:08,396 --> 00:02:11,439
Then the hard part of the brief.

33
00:02:11,889 --> 00:02:15,802
Each job gets one thing nobody else can do.

34
00:02:16,702 --> 00:02:19,746
There are two ways to write that.

35
00:02:20,196 --> 00:02:24,543
A skill on an answer, or needs on a prop.

36
00:02:25,443 --> 00:02:27,617
It can't be a job,

37
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:32,415
because a job is covered by whoever's in the scene.

38
00:02:34,215 --> 00:02:37,693
And here's the rule that keeps it fair.

39
00:02:38,593 --> 00:02:41,637
A thing only one person can do

40
00:02:42,087 --> 00:02:44,696
must never be the only road.

41
00:02:46,496 --> 00:02:49,974
So the cheap ending is open to anybody.

42
00:02:50,874 --> 00:02:53,483
The good ending has two doors,

43
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:56,107
and each one needs somebody.

44
00:02:57,307 --> 00:02:59,046
Now the quest tree.

45
00:02:59,496 --> 00:03:04,278
Remember what the bridge gets: the shared quests, and nothing else.

46
00:03:05,178 --> 00:03:09,091
So this tree is the story the bridge follows.

47
00:03:10,891 --> 00:03:13,935
One arc, with the clock on it.

48
00:03:14,835 --> 00:03:20,052
The arc waits, and the first answer on the ground starts it.

49
00:03:20,502 --> 00:03:23,546
So nobody loses time choosing a console.

50
00:03:25,346 --> 00:03:28,389
Each step is news for the ship.

51
00:03:29,289 --> 00:03:33,202
And the two endings are the last two steps,

52
00:03:33,652 --> 00:03:36,261
each with its own winning sentence.

53
00:03:38,061 --> 00:03:41,104
I got this wrong the first time.

54
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:44,598
I had the endings outside the arc.

55
00:03:45,498 --> 00:03:49,846
The arc finished early, and the clock stopped with it.

56
00:03:50,296 --> 00:03:52,904
Keep the endings inside, and waiting.

57
00:03:54,104 --> 00:03:56,713
Both endings live in one room.

58
00:03:57,613 --> 00:03:59,787
A choice has one condition,

59
00:04:00,237 --> 00:04:04,150
so a thing that needs two takes two rooms.

60
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:08,948
Facts in the first, and the jacks in the second.

61
00:04:10,748 --> 00:04:13,791
Now something you have to plan for.

62
00:04:14,691 --> 00:04:18,170
A full shot destroys any prop it hits.

63
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:22,533
The game doesn't stop, and it doesn't tell anyone.

64
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:28,680
Shoot the lift gate, and you can walk through it.

65
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:33,493
Shoot the rock fall, and no ending is left.

66
00:04:35,293 --> 00:04:38,772
So ask two questions of your own mission.

67
00:04:39,222 --> 00:04:41,396
Which props hold an ending?

68
00:04:41,846 --> 00:04:45,324
And which doors does only a signal open?

69
00:04:47,124 --> 00:04:50,602
Mine still ends, because the clock runs out.

70
00:04:51,052 --> 00:04:54,096
That's the best reason to have one.

71
00:04:55,296 --> 00:04:57,035
Lint reads your spelling.

72
00:04:57,485 --> 00:04:59,659
It doesn't walk your map.

73
00:05:00,559 --> 00:05:05,776
So here are the checks of the whole class, on one sheet.

74
00:05:06,226 --> 00:05:08,400
Twelve of them, in order.

75
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,374
Ways in and ways out.

76
00:05:12,824 --> 00:05:14,998
Keys and names that join.

77
00:05:15,448 --> 00:05:17,187
Signals with two ends.

78
00:05:18,087 --> 00:05:21,565
Then the worst party, and the three columns.

79
00:05:22,015 --> 00:05:25,493
The screen, a full shot, and the clock.

80
00:05:27,293 --> 00:05:29,467
Then walk it, every road.

81
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:32,541
Three people dig them out.

82
00:05:33,441 --> 00:05:37,789
One person, with no skill at all, blasts them out.

83
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:43,937
The times on the page are floors from a script.

84
00:05:44,387 --> 00:05:48,735
Walk yours with people, and write down what you get.

85
00:05:49,935 --> 00:05:52,543
Here's the rubric, in ten lines,

86
00:05:52,993 --> 00:05:56,472
and each one has a way to know.

87
00:05:58,272 --> 00:06:03,489
Three areas. A quest tree. Two endings and a way to lose.

88
00:06:04,389 --> 00:06:06,563
Three jobs nobody can replace.

89
00:06:07,013 --> 00:06:10,057
A clock that starts on the ground.

90
00:06:10,957 --> 00:06:13,565
An ending for the smallest party.

91
00:06:14,015 --> 00:06:16,624
And work for three at once.

92
00:06:18,424 --> 00:06:21,467
You're done when every line is ticked,

93
00:06:21,917 --> 00:06:24,961
and when somebody who didn't write it

94
00:06:25,411 --> 00:06:29,759
has played it to an ending without asking you anything.

95
00:06:31,559 --> 00:06:34,167
That's the end of Boarding Parties.

96
00:06:34,617 --> 00:06:36,791
Now go and write yours.
